00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.327
A zero-to-one consumer app, shipped in six months — and switched off within months of launch.

2
00:00:07.328 --> 00:00:10.256
It's on my portfolio anyway.

3
00:00:10.257 --> 00:00:12.744
The reason why is the point.

4
00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:23.858
Crowd data collapsed into one quietness score, one to ten, with a British voice — designed for anxious travellers, not commuters.

5
00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:28.050
Even the error state became a reason to come back.

6
00:00:28.051 --> 00:00:38.025
It ran on the AdTech platform's own footfall data — the same infrastructure from the biggest case on this site, pointed at consumers.

7
00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:45.273
When the reason people won't act is emotional, the interface is where you pay it — not the model.

8
00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:53.255
The numbers, honestly small: zero usability complaints, with no tutorial shipped.

9
00:00:53.256 --> 00:00:59.921
Two hundred and fifty monthly actives on a thousand visitors — a small, loyal base.

10
00:00:59.922 --> 00:01:07.018
Designer and strategist on a small remote client team, July to December twenty-twenty-one.

11
00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:11.741
And where it breaks — because it did.

12
00:01:11.742 --> 00:01:20.296
Warmth can't rescue a weak signal: a mascot on top of bad data is a lie with a face on it.

13
00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:23.310
And charm is not a moat.

14
00:01:23.311 --> 00:01:27.144
PlanIt was switched off within months.

15
